# Standardized terminology

Details: `doc/i18n.rst`.

ICAO abbreviations and codes stay as published in Doc 8400. Do not pass
the abbreviation itself through gettext.

Examples: `IAS`, `TAS`, `CAS`, `EAS`, `QNH`, `QFE`, `QNE`, `IFR`, `VFR`,
`VMC`, `IMC`.

- The abbreviation is a string literal: `"TAS"`, `"IAS"`.
- Do not add a msgid that is only that abbreviation (`_("TAS")`,
  `N_("IAS")`, `C_("Abbreviation", "TAS")`).
- A sentence around it is ordinary language and stays in `_()` / `N_()`.
  Translators keep the abbreviation unchanged inside the sentence.
- Leave abbreviations that are already in the catalogs alone. Do not
  start a cleanup unless asked.

Brand names stay as published. Examples: `WeGlide`, `SoaringScoring`,
`SkySight`, `XC Therm`, `NetCDF`. A label that is only the name is a literal. A
sentence around it still translates, and the name stays unchanged
inside that sentence.

```cpp
// BAD: the abbreviation becomes a translatable string
data.FmtComment("{} {}", speed, C_("Abbreviation", "TAS"));

// GOOD: the label is fixed; the help sentence still translates
AddBoolean("IAS",
           _("Show the speed-to-fly as indicated airspeed."),
           on, listener);
data.FmtComment("{} {}", speed, "TAS");
```
